text:
The premise of Oxygen Not Included is to expand your colony on a alien asteroid and make the best out of the situation. You start with 3 Duplicants and it's very important to select a good team. The Dupes' are very hardworking will do whatever you tell them to do. The game is deceptively cute at first until your Dupes get sick, your base starts to crumble and everyone dies of a horrible disease, then it gets very, very grim. RIP Bubbles.
Oxygen Not Included is from the creators of Don't Starve and as such it bears some similarities - they're both difficult, centred around base building and survival, and require precise resource management. Both games are very unforgiving, and both lack an end goal.
I really enjoy this game, but I can see why some people dislike it. If you're not a fan of designing systems and seeing them fail miserably a couple of times, then you might find this game frustrating.
Pros:
Unique art style;
Amazing ambient soundtrack;
Different base building strategies are possible;
Somewhat elaborate base building;
Addicting;
Cheap even at full price;
Reliable developer - frequent updates.
Cons:
No end game;
No proper tutorial - you will need to figure things on your own;
Dupes are dumb as hell;
Can get frustrating;
Weird game logic at times - most buildings do not work the way you think they do.
My current rating: 8/10. Pick up this game if you enjoy some struggle.

